# Fixed interface facts (identical for every arm)

The implementation must satisfy these surfaces exactly. Everything else is a design decision.

## `bin/lib/codeops-rpc.mjs` (new) — declarations for `bin/lib/codeops-rpc.d.mts`

```ts
@@CODEOPS_RPC_DTS@@```

## Behavior pinned by acceptance

- `registerCodeOpsRpc(ctx, { pluginVersion })` resolves to `false` and never throws when `ctx.rpc`
  is missing, `ctx.rpc` is `{}`, `ctx.rpc.register` is not a function, or `register` rejects. On
  success it resolves to `true` after registering a definition whose `id` is `"codeops"` with a
  `status` handler that returns exactly `{ pluginVersion, openCodeVersion: ctx.app.version,
  directory: ctx.location.directory }` (all strings).
- `plugin/index.ts` registers only through `registerCodeOpsRpc`, inside `try { … } catch`, reports
  failure through the existing `warnContentFree(…)`, and never calls `.rpc.register` directly.
  `setup` keeps all existing hooks with and without the RPC API.
- `plugin/tui.tsx` (new, `./tui` entry): claims the slot with `append: "sidebar.content"`, imports
  from `../bin/lib/codeops-rpc.mjs`, renders only a payload validated by `isCodeOpsStatus`, uses no
  `setInterval`/`setTimeout`, and contains the strip text `CodeOps v` exactly once.
- `package.json`: `exports["./tui"]` is `"./plugin/tui.tsx"`; `files` contains `plugin/`,
  `!plugin/*.test.mjs`, and `!plugin/*.spec.test.mjs`; `npm pack --dry-run` ships `plugin/tui.tsx`
  and no plugin test file.
